<Slide style={{
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    background: '#FFFFFF',
    padding: '60px 60px',
    flexDirection: 'column',
    fontFamily: '"Arial", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif',
}}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#3D7BD9', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.6 }}>
        H4 · RQ2 — IS THE GAP A CALIBRATION DEFECT?
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#0E3F8C', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 10 }}>
        Information, not calibration
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ height: 1, background: '#D6DCE5', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flex: 1, justifyContent: 'center', flexDirection: 'row', gap: 44, alignItems: 'center' }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 616 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568' }}>
                Change in the gap after re-calibrating the market against itself
            </Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'flex-end', gap: 12, marginTop: 6 }}>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 46, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>0.0019</Text>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#4A5568' }}>relative, 90% CI [−0.0085, +0.0127]</Text>
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#1A2230', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
                The whole interval sits below the 0.25 decision line — re-calibration explains
                almost none of the gap.
            </Text>

            <Box style={{ marginTop: 22, padding: '14px 18px', background: '#F7F9FC', border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', borderRadius: 6 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'flex-end', gap: 10 }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 30, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#8B97A8' }}>8.7%</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568' }}>upper bound, open-book oracle</Text>
                </Box>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.55, marginTop: 6 }}>
                    Fitting both parameters on the test labels — cheating — still recovers less than a
                    tenth of the gap. So the gap is information the models do not have.
                </Text>
            </Box>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ width: 500, justifyContent: 'center' }}>
            <Image src="assets/fig08_right.png" style={{ width: 440, height: 344 }} />
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ padding: '12px 20px', background: '#F0F5FC', borderRadius: 6 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
            If the gap were a calibration defect, fixing the market's own calibration would close it.
            It does not: 0.0019 against a 0.25 decision line, and 8.7% even with the test labels.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>DSC5001 · Statistical Machine Learning I</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Team 32 · 8/10</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
